To transform the mock-up into a colorful website with real jokes, you can use HTML and JavaScript. Below is a simple example of how you might structure it:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            color: #333;
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .joke {
            background-color: #fff;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        h1 {
            color: #666;
        }
        button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    <div class="joke">
        <p>Why don't scientists trust atoms?</p>
        <button onclick="showPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
        <p id="joke1-punchline" style="display:none;">Because they make up everything!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="joke">
        <p>What do you call a fake noodle?</p>
        <button onclick="showPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
        <p id="joke2-punchline" style="display:none;">An impasta!</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        function showPunchline() {
            var joke = document.getElementById('joke1-punchline');
            if (joke.style.display === 'none') {
                joke.style.display = 'block';
            } else {
                joke.style.display = 'none';
            }
        }

Here's a simple HTML/JavaScript code snippet to create an interactive joke website based on your mock-up:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .joke-container {
            border: 2px solid blue;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: white;
            width: 80%;
            text-align: center;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .joke-container h1 {
            color: blue;
        }
        .joke-container p {
            color: black;
            font-style: italic;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <p id="joke">[Funny Joke]</p>
        <button onclick="revealPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline() {
            const jokeElement = document.getElementById('joke');
            jokeElement.textContent = "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a basic webpage with a centered joke container that displays a joke when the button is clicked. The joke is hardcoded for demonstration purposes; you can replace it with a real joke or a joke API call if needed.
